(1894, 'long', '/lɒŋ/', 'adjective', '{"zh-TW":["【主要意義-形容詞/副詞】長的；長時間的","【次要意義-動詞】渴望；切望；強烈希望得到"],"en":["[primary] measuring a great distance or duration","[secondary - verb] to have a strong desire or wish for something"]}', NULL, 'long for / long to do / long-awaited', '[{"en":"The team longed for a resolution to the prolonged contract dispute.","zh-TW":"團隊渴望解決長期的合約糾紛。"},{"en":"Employees longed for more flexible working arrangements.","zh-TW":"員工渴望更靈活的工作安排。"},{"en":"She had long longed for the opportunity to lead her own project.","zh-TW":"她長久以來一直渴望有機會主導自己的專案。"}]', '{"noun":"longing","adjective":"longing"}', '動詞 long for = 「渴望」，是正式書面英語中的高階詞彙，相當於 yearn for，在 TOEIC 閱讀描述員工情感或職涯期望的語境中偶爾出現。', 1, 1894, NULL),
